## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Complete

### Summary
Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for the url-shortener-web Next.js application following the latest official Vercel documentation.

### Changes Made

#### Modified Files:
- **apps/url-shortener-web/app/layout.tsx** - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout

### Implementation Details

1. **Documentation Review**: Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart to ensure up-to-date configuration steps.

2. **Framework Identification**: Confirmed this is a Next.js 16.3.0 application using the App Router pattern.

3. **Package Status**: The `@vercel/analytics` package (v2.0.1) was already installed in the project dependencies, as confirmed in package.json.

4. **Component Integration**: Added the `<Analytics />` component to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) inside the `<body>` tag, following the official Next.js App Router integration pattern. The import statement was already present at the top of the file.

5. **Build Verification**: Successfully built the application with `pnpm build` to verify no TypeScript or compilation errors were introduced.

6. **Linter Check**: Ran the linter which showed pre-existing issues in other files (ShortenWidget.tsx, ThemeToggle.tsx, proxy.ts) unrelated to the Analytics integration. The Analytics component change itself introduces no linting errors.

### Technical Notes

- The Analytics component is now rendered at the end of the body tag, which is the recommended placement for optimal performance and tracking accuracy.
- The component will automatically track page views and web vitals once the application is deployed to Vercel.
- No additional configuration is required in next.config.ts as per the documentation.
- The integration follows the official Vercel Web Analytics best practices for Next.js App Router applications.

### Next Steps for Deployment

According to the official documentation, to complete the setup:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings > Analytics > Enable)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Verify tracking is working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

The code changes are ready for deployment and will begin tracking analytics once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
